  "claims": [
    "Any explicit HigherBasis can be closed under the four mixed placements. Generator support and both boundary inclusions are tracked recursively. No missing critical generators are synthesized by this closure.",
    "Embedding an old higher cell in the contextual closure preserves its declared support and Four-constructor count. Whiskering adds exactly the placement needs and preserves that count. Fresh requirements distribute over this union.",
    "The concrete completed MAC catalogue has eleven explicit local higher-diagram forms: separated exchange, the prior completion definition, association naturality in three arguments, the associativity pentagon, sequential-wire fusion naturality in two arguments, tensor-wire fusion naturality in two arguments, and suffix-completion naturality in its continuation.",
    "Association naturality retains the actual changed-step support, including comparison-only guards, together with the other two argument needs. The pentagon retains the four argument needs. Pure-wire fusion naturality has empty guard support. Suffix naturality retains {n,n+1} union the changed-continuation step support.",
    "The prior completion higher cells can be translated into this common contextual presentation with exactly preserved support and Four-constructor count.",
    "The prior actual mixed association/MAC critical cell now lifts through arbitrary mixed placements. Its support is exactly {n,n+1} union continuation needs union placement needs. Kernel repair with arbitrary correlated prior data and retained input uses only the updated checked old-catalogue model via conservative extension.",
    "At every stage n, placing untouched before(n+2) beside the mixed critical cell, then copying or discarding the resulting bundle, preserves support {n,n+1,n+2}; the Four-constructor count is twelve and fresh support for changed ID {n+3} is empty."
  ],
