  "limits": [
    "The eleven diagram tags are a catalogue of implemented forms, NOT a proved exhaustive classifier for all critical overlaps. Each is a parameterized family with generally infinitely many typed instances.",
    "A complete pure-wire higher presentation, association against sequential-fusion roots, association against nested suffix roots, and an exhaustive classification/generation theorem for all mixed overlaps remain to be established. Some missing cells may be derivable from the presented ones, but such derivations are not claimed here.",
    "No global termination, confluence, complete finite mixed homotopy basis, or arbitrary parallel-track coherence is proved for the enlarged catalogue. Context closure alone cannot supply these results.",
    "Four-constructor counting excludes boundary tracks, wires, circuit syntax, guard data, context witnesses and shared libraries. Context placement is stored inside generator payloads and may enlarge total data even while this count is preserved.",
    "Support is conservative and syntactic. Empty fresh guard support is not a measured cost or a proof that external semantic checking takes zero time. No minimal-condition theorem or independent ordinary-proof total-cost comparison is supplied.",
    "Joint repair compares two circuits in the same updated checked model and retains correlated prior data. It does not equate old and revised model distributions, turn structural proof inverses into stochastic inverses, or clone mutable oracle executions.",
    "The existing MAC kernels, full state/trace and indexed security conditions are unchanged. No new attack, cryptographic bound, computational reduction implementation, native continuing-machine guarantee, or runtime result is added."
  ],
